  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1142 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nMonday through Thursday:\n\nBrief WAA behind the Sunday cold front will keep temperatures\nabove normal in the upper 50s to near 60s on Monday. Then,\nseries of dry troughs this week and relative high pressure will\nkeep precipitation at bay much of this week amid a mix of sun\nand clouds. The latter part of the extended period has trended\ncolder as a stronger cold front and Canadian high are expected\nto move out of central Canada into the upper Great Lakes region\nlate this week. This will lead to temperatures at or slightly\nbelow normal for Thursday and Friday. Some lake effect rain\nshowers may occur along the lakeshore on Thursday (15 to 30%\nchances) as favorable fetch and delta-T's will induce lake \ndriven convection.\n\nCMiller",
